-- ALPreps bracketology — the hand-authored layer, as one document.
--
-- Generated by scripts/make-bracket-sql.ts from the old bracketology site's
-- export. Paste this into the Supabase SQL editor; no local tooling needed.
--
-- What is in it: 8 classifications' brackets, 30 region
-- write-ups, 208 projected winners, 112 game notes,
-- 73 status overrides, the news note, and the explainer.
--
-- What is deliberately NOT in it: records, seed order and status. Those are
-- computed from the games and the ratings on every render, so a copy stored
-- here would be a second answer to a question the site already answers.
--
-- The bracket stores places — {"region": 4, "place": 2} — never team names, so
-- re-seeding a region moves every slot that refers to it without this document
-- changing at all.
--
-- Safe to run more than once: it replaces row 1 outright.

do $$
begin
  if to_regclass('public.bracket') is null then
    raise exception
      'public.bracket was not found in database "%". Run '
      'supabase/migrations/006_bracket.sql first.', current_database();
  end if;
end $$;

insert into public.bracket (id, data)
values (1, '{"season":"2026","newsNote":"All classifications are updated through Week 4 (9/18/26). We aren''t projecting much yet, so some teams may be higher or lower than expected based on limited results. However, there are some projects in the bigger classifications. Follow us on X @ALPreps for more info!","aboutHtml":"<h2>What is bracketology?</h2>\nBracketology is the practice of projecting a postseason field before it is actually set. It was started by Joe Lunardi back in the 90''s as a way to predict the participants that would make the NCAA Basketball tournament each year. Back in 2016, I started this process with Alabama high school football and I''ve done it every year since.\n\nInstead of waiting for the AHSAA to release the official brackets, we take what we know right now — region standings, results so far, and who still has to play whom — and build the bracket based on those factors. It is part math, part opinion, and it changes every week. \n\n<h2>How the AHSAA playoff field works</h2>\nAlabama does not use one big statewide seeding. Every classification is split into regions, and teams qualify out of their own region. Where you finish in your region is the only thing that matters — a 7-3 team can finish ahead of an 8-2 team if their region record is better.\n\nThe field is different in each classification:\n\n<b>Class 6A</b> — 4 regions, top 6 from each region qualify (24 teams). The top 2 seeds in each region get a first-round bye straight into the second round. The regions rotate who plays who each year and is not based on geography.\n<b>Classes 1A–5A</b> — 8 regions each, top 4 from each region qualify (32 teams). Regions 1-4 are in the south and regions 5-8 are in the north.\n<b>Class AA (private)</b> — 2 regions, the whole field qualifies (16 teams). Each region plays itself down to a winner that advances to the championship.\n<b>Class A (private)</b> — 4 regions, top 4 from each region qualify (16 teams). Regions 1-2 are in the south and regions 3-4 are in the north.\n\n<h2>How to read the bracket</h2>\nEvery team on the bracket carries a seed tag on the left, written like <b>R4-2</b>. That means <i>the second-place team out of Region 4</i>. <b>It is not that team''s record.</b> The tag travels with the team as it advances, so you can always see where somebody came from.\n\nA few other things worth knowing:\n\n- An <b>H</b> next to a team means they are the home team for that game.\n- A blank slot next to a team means they have a <b>bye</b> — nobody to play that round, and they advance automatically.\n- <b>Click any game</b> to see the date, time, location, and both teams’ records. This won''t be fully filled in until the bracket and match-ups are set.\n\n<h2>Region standings and status colors</h2>\nThe Region Standings tab shows every team in playoff order, with their overall record and their region record. Region record is what actually decides seeding.\n\nEach team also carries a status showing how safe their playoff position is:\n\n<b><span style=\"color:#1d4ed8\">Clinched</span></b> — Mathematically locked into that spot, regardless of what happens next.\n<b><span style=\"color:#1f9d4d\">High</span></b> — High confidence that the team will most likely will finish close to where they are now.\n<b><span style=\"color:#ff751f\">Medium</span></b> — Medium confidence that the team will most likely will finish within a spot or two of where our projections have them.\n<b><span style=\"color:#d60000\">Low</span></b> — May be in good position now, but low confidence that they end up in that spot, or even in the playoffs at as things could drastically change with just one or two results.\n<b><span style=\"color:#58595b\">Out</span></b> — Eliminated from playoff contention, either mathematically or we just think it''s too high of a ladder to climb.\n\n<h2>Some notes about the info on this site</h2>\n\n– This is all based on a few factors: A) current region record, B) strength of region record to that point, C) non-region record, which is only used for tiebreak purposes, and D) my own opinions and projections. Most teams will be placed based on their region record at that point, but sometimes we may make a change based on our opinion of what we believe will happen in the future. When we do give our opinion or our own projections, we will note that. Some teams start with a harder path than others so they aren''t as high as you think they probably should be. \n\n– When it comes to non-region wins and tiebreakers, the most important thing to remember is – the <b>quality</b> of non-region wins means more than the <b>quantity</b> of non-region wins. For instance, Team A with a 1-2 non-region record can be ahead of Team B with a 3-0 non-region record if the one team that Team A beat has more wins than the 3 teams combined that Team B defeated.\n\n– It’s also important to note that a team can’t lose a tiebreaker, only win it. For instance, if three teams beat each other within the season to cause a 3-way tie, and it goes to non-region wins or some other tiebreaker where one team is clearly out of the running to win it, then that doesn’t mean they are out of the running if there are more playoff spots to get. Teams with bad records are rewarded for their region wins just like teams with good records are punished for their region losses.\n\n– There have recently been some different interpretations of wording in the rule book when it comes to tiebreakers between schools and the AHSAA. We can only go off how we interpret the words that are written and past precedent in similar scenarios. We may get something wrong based on our interpretation, and if so – don’t forget that the AHSAA has the final word and whatever they say goes, whether we like it or not.\n\n<h2>About the projections</h2>\nFlip on <b>Show projected results</b> on any bracket to see it filled out the rest of the way. This is based on ratings and projections from a few different sites.\n\nThey will be wrong sometimes. That is the nature of it.\n\n<h2>A note on accuracy</h2>\nThis is an independent project and is not affiliated with the AHSAA. Brackets here are projections until the AHSAA releases the official pairings. Standings and results are updated by hand, so if you spot something wrong, let us know.","aboutBanner":{"enabled":true,"text":"New to bracketology? Learn how these brackets, seeds and projections work."},"showProjections":true,"classes":{"6A":{"alignment":[1,2,3,4],"slots":[{"region":4,"place":1},null,{"region":3,"place":4},{"region":4,"place":5},{"region":2,"place":2},null,{"region":1,"place":3},{"region":2,"place":6},{"region":3,"place":1},null,{"region":4,"place":4},{"region":3,"place":5},{"region":1,"place":2},null,{"region":2,"place":3},{"region":1,"place":6},{"region":2,"place":1},null,{"region":1,"place":4},{"region":2,"place":5},{"region":4,"place":2},null,{"region":3,"place":3},{"region":4,"place":6},{"region":1,"place":1},null,{"region":2,"place":4},{"region":1,"place":5},{"region":3,"place":2},null,{"region":4,"place":3},{"region":3,"place":6}],"results":{"r1g1":{"home":"top"},"r1g3":{"home":"top"},"r1g5":{"home":"top"},"r1g7":{"home":"top"},"r1g9":{"home":"top"},"r1g11":{"home":"top"},"r1g13":{"home":"top"},"r1g15":{"home":"top"},"r2g0":{"home":"top"},"r2g1":{"home":"top"},"r2g2":{"home":"top"},"r2g3":{"home":"top"},"r2g4":{"home":"top"},"r2g5":{"home":"top"},"r2g6":{"home":"top"},"r2g7":{"home":"top"}},"projected":{"r2g0":"bottom","r1g1":"top","r1g3":"bottom","r1g5":"bottom","r1g7":"top","r1g9":"bottom","r1g11":"top","r1g13":"top","r1g15":"bottom","r2g7":"top","r2g6":"bottom","r2g5":"bottom","r2g4":"top","r3g2":"top","r3g3":"bottom","r4g1":"top","r2g3":"bottom","r2g2":"top","r2g1":"top","r3g0":"top","r3g1":"top","r4g0":"bottom","r5g0":"top"},"regions":{"1":{"note":"Don''t forget that Mary Montgomery''s games don''t count toward championship play and they are banned from the postseason.\n\nFairhope and Daphne are the favorites right now for the first round bye, but Foley got a big win over Baker to put themselves in the conversation.","status":{"Mary Montgomery":"out"}},"2":{"note":"Central continues to remain the team to beat, but there is still a good fight going on behind them.\n\nAfter the region break, we get Auburn at Opelika to give us an idea of who is the favorite for second and that coveted bye week.","status":{"Smiths Station":"low"}},"3":{"note":"Too early to tell. But yes, we''ve moved Thompson to high because they have been absolutely dominant.\n\nThompson and Prattville have separated themselves as the top 2 teams. Prattville got a dominant 63-30 win over Hewitt and Vestavia took it to Spain Park. Still games to play, but it''s shaking out something close to this.\n\nA lot of these teams will be off next week as region play takes a break, but then we get Thompson at Hoover, and Spain Park at Prattville to help us see a little clearer.","status":{"Thompson":"high","Tuscaloosa County":"low"}},"4":{"note":"Counting down until the James Clemens at Sparkman game on October 9. Bob Jones beat Buckhorn to give them that tiebreaker.","status":{"Grissom":"low","Hazel Green":"low"}}}},"5A":{"alignment":[1,4,2,3,5,6,7,8],"slots":[{"region":4,"place":1},{"region":1,"place":4},{"region":2,"place":2},{"region":3,"place":3},{"region":1,"place":1},{"region":4,"place":4},{"region":3,"place":2},{"region":2,"place":3},{"region":3,"place":1},{"region":2,"place":4},{"region":1,"place":2},{"region":4,"place":3},{"region":2,"place":1},{"region":3,"place":4},{"region":4,"place":2},{"region":1,"place":3},{"region":8,"place":1},{"region":5,"place":4},{"region":6,"place":2},{"region":7,"place":3},{"region":5,"place":1},{"region":8,"place":4},{"region":7,"place":2},{"region":6,"place":3},{"region":7,"place":1},{"region":6,"place":4},{"region":5,"place":2},{"region":8,"place":3},{"region":6,"place":1},{"region":7,"place":4},{"region":8,"place":2},{"region":5,"place":3}],"results":{"r1g0":{"home":"top"},"r1g1":{"home":"top"},"r1g2":{"home":"top"},"r1g3":{"home":"top"},"r1g4":{"home":"top"},"r1g5":{"home":"top"},"r1g6":{"home":"top"},"r1g7":{"home":"top"},"r1g8":{"home":"top"},"r1g9":{"home":"top"},"r1g10":{"home":"top"},"r1g11":{"home":"top"},"r1g12":{"home":"top"},"r1g13":{"home":"top"},"r1g14":{"home":"top"},"r1g15":{"home":"top"}},"projected":{"r1g0":"top","r1g1":"top","r1g2":"top","r1g3":"top","r1g4":"top","r1g5":"bottom","r1g6":"top","r1g7":"bottom","r1g8":"top","r1g9":"bottom","r1g10":"top","r1g11":"top","r1g12":"top","r1g13":"top","r1g14":"top","r1g15":"top","r2g7":"top","r2g6":"top","r2g5":"top","r2g4":"bottom","r2g3":"bottom","r2g2":"top","r2g1":"bottom","r2g0":"top","r3g0":"top","r3g1":"top","r4g0":"bottom","r3g3":"bottom","r3g2":"bottom","r4g1":"bottom","r5g0":"top"},"regions":{"1":{"note":"Gulf Shores already has a big win over Saraland, but Spanish Fort still has to play both. The Toros face Gulf Shores on October 16, and Saraland the next week in the final week of region play.\n\nBehind them, Theodore is leading now for the fourth spot but face Blount after their bye week and still have Spanish Fort and Gulf Shores.","status":{"Gulf Shores":"high","Baldwin County":"low","Elberta":"low"}},"2":{"note":"Pike Road and Benjamin Russell are now set to face off for sole possession of first place on October 9th. Pike Road gets Russell County before that though and Wetumpka after.\n\nThis region did not look good in Week 5 with 3 of the top 4 losing.","status":{"Pike Road":"low","Benjamin Russell":"low","Park Crossing":"low","Stanhope Elmore":"low"}},"3":{"note":"Hillcrest may be the best team in 5A this year the way they are playing so far, but you can''t count McAdory out. Those two teams face off on October 9th at Hillcrest.\n\nIt''s a battle behind them to determine 3rd and 4th and we need to let it play out. Central and Bessemer City have pulled a game ahead and they face off October 9th as well.","status":{"Hillcrest-Tuscaloosa":"high","McAdory":"high","Brookwood":"low","Hueytown":"low"}},"4":{"note":"Calera dropped their first game of the season to Ramsay, which has now set up a big game between the Rams and Mountain Brook when region play returns. A Ramsay win will knock Mountain Brook to playing for third and set up a region title game between Homewood and Ramsay in the final week. A Mountain Brook win will make it where a Ramsay win over Homewood will cause a 3-way tie, which as of right now would go to Homewood (based on non-region tiebreakers).\n\nHelena fell to Homewood but still has that win over Pelham to help them. It could come down to Calera vs Helena at the end to determine who is fourth, but Pelham is not out of it.","status":{"Homewood":"high","Ramsay":"high","Chelsea":"low","Chilton County":"low"}},"5":{"note":"Parker is Parker, no shock they are in first. They already beat Mortimer Jordan and Minor behind them. They end with Gardendale.\n\nBehind them, it''s a fight to see who will be teams 3 and 4. Mortimer Jordan beat Gardendale who beat Jasper so we''ve got it in that order for now. Minor/Cullman/Huffman could still challenge for a final spot .","status":{"Parker":"high","Jackson-Olin":"low"}},"6":{"note":"Clay got up on Oxford and claimed their spot at the top alone...again\n\nPell City got a big win in appeals and a big win on the field over St. Clair County and just like that - they are sitting in third place. They still need to get a win over Southside to be comfortably in, but they are looking good for now. We don''t know a lot about Southside yet because their only games are a loss to Clay and a win over Pinson, but they will for a spot too. So for now we have them fifth. St. Clair County and Southside could be fighting for the final spot in the final week of region play.","status":{"Clay-Chalkville":"high","Springville":"low","Pinson Valley":"low"}},"7":{"note":"This is a tough region with six playoff teams coming together in reclassification.\n\nFlorence has looked really strong this season, already getting wins now in region over Muscle Shoals and Russellville. \n\nRussellville and Muscle Shoals will play when we get back to region play on October 2. Muscle Shoals beat Austin who beat Athens, so we''ve got Athens on the outside looking in at the moment. \n\nHartselle dropped games to Russellville and Muscle Shoals, so they still have a chance to get back into it.","status":{"Decatur":"low","East Limestone":"low"}},"8":{"note":"The season is looking hopefully for five teams right now, but the rest of region play will have to eliminate one of these teams. Douglas beat Mae Jemison who beat Fort Payne which is why Fort Payne is currently on the outside looking in. Douglas travels to Fort Payne on October 16. \n\nMeanwhile, Arab travels to Boaz that same weekend so we will know a lot more then.","status":{"Albertville":"low","Columbia":"low","Lee-Huntsville":"low"}}}},"4A":{"alignment":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],"slots":[{"region":4,"place":1},{"region":1,"place":4},{"region":2,"place":2},{"region":3,"place":3},{"region":1,"place":1},{"region":4,"place":4},{"region":3,"place":2},{"region":2,"place":3},{"region":3,"place":1},{"region":2,"place":4},{"region":1,"place":2},{"region":4,"place":3},{"region":2,"place":1},{"region":3,"place":4},{"region":4,"place":2},{"region":1,"place":3},{"region":8,"place":1},{"region":5,"place":4},{"region":6,"place":2},{"region":7,"place":3},{"region":5,"place":1},{"region":8,"place":4},{"region":7,"place":2},{"region":6,"place":3},{"region":7,"place":1},{"region":6,"place":4},{"region":5,"place":2},{"region":8,"place":3},{"region":6,"place":1},{"region":7,"place":4},{"region":8,"place":2},{"region":5,"place":3}],"results":{"r1g0":{"home":"top"},"r1g1":{"home":"top"},"r1g2":{"home":"top"},"r1g3":{"home":"top"},"r1g4":{"home":"top"},"r1g5":{"home":"top"},"r1g6":{"home":"top"},"r1g7":{"home":"top"},"r1g8":{"home":"top"},"r1g9":{"home":"top"},"r1g10":{"home":"top"},"r1g11":{"home":"top"},"r1g12":{"home":"top"},"r1g13":{"home":"top"},"r1g14":{"home":"top"},"r1